{title: Be Now Our Shepherd}
{artist: Larry Holder}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 80}

Verse 1
and let me know what you think of this song or this method
of outreach.

Verse 2
This song was written by request especially for
Church is Sacred Heart in Woonsocket, Rhode Island,
to celebrate the arrival of their new pastor and his
25 years of service in the ministry. As many of you
know, "pastor" is Spanish for "shepherd", so in this
song, shepherd is referring to the minister.

Verse 3
"Be Now Our Shepherd"
Words and Music by Lawrence Keith Holder
Copyright © 2001 Lawrence Keith Holder

Verse 4
(chorus)
Be now our shepherd, breaking the Bread of Life,
and feeding God's children.
Leading us on as we worship the Risen Lord
and serve Him forever.

Verse 5
(verse 1)
We thank the Almighty and open our hearts,
receiving you gladly in truth and in love.
Your faithful obedience in serving the Lord
reflecting the grace of our Father above.

Verse 6
(chorus again)

Verse 7
(verse 2)
We join now together of one heart and mind,
to live for the Lord as we serve by your side.
And Jesus Himself is our witness today,
for where two or three gather, His Spirit abides.

Verse 8
(chorus again, adding 2nd voice, which is...)

Verse 9
...Be now our shepherd,
breaking the Bread with God's children.
...Leading us onward,
serving the Savior forever.

Verse 10
(chorus again, key change from D to E)

Verse 11
(ending)
All praise to our Father above!
